abstract: 'Version 0.2.0 of the 1868 Bodleian Sinica2021 witness: 398 original-print
  units, 6536 Unicode code points, 35 text uncertainties and 35 reviewed unresolved
  source regions. The same two reader groups made source-only observations in fresh
  native contexts, sealed their independent drafts, and then continued in those original
  contexts with non-blind source adjudication. These are two stages of activity by
  the same readers. Changed, added, split and removed units are disclosed with source
  reasons; they are not accuracy estimates. No human double collation, expert review
  or peer review is claimed. Native model, effort and counters remain unknown.'
